1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,112
Narrator: Scenario 72. Incident response.

2
00:00:05,712 --> 00:00:16,224
A: Checkout failures are confirmed in two regions, with thirty percent of attempts failing over ten minutes. This appears to meet our major-incident criteria.

3
00:00:16,824 --> 00:00:26,712
B: What evidence supports that assessment, and which parts of the customer journey remain available? I need the current scope before assigning the severity.

4
00:00:27,312 --> 00:00:39,648
A: External checkout tests and production transaction records agree. Browsing and existing order lookup remain available; unique affected customer counts are still being validated.

5
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:51,120
C: Application logs show payment confirmation timeouts. We have not determined whether the cause is in our code, the database, or the network path.

6
00:00:51,720 --> 00:01:04,104
B: Under our documented impact criteria, I am declaring severity one and opening the major-incident bridge. Please record 14:12 UTC as the declaration time.

7
00:01:04,704 --> 00:01:14,352
A: I will page the application, database, and network on-call engineers through the escalation system, with the incident link and confirmed facts attached.

8
00:01:14,952 --> 00:01:25,848
B: Ask each team to acknowledge ownership, not simply join the call. If anyone misses the policy response window, use the documented backup escalation.

9
00:01:26,448 --> 00:01:37,584
C: I accept the application investigation. I will compare failing and successful requests and check recent changes while preserving samples for the other teams.

10
00:01:38,184 --> 00:01:48,648
A: The database engineer has acknowledged; the network page is still pending. I am tracking both response times and will escalate if the window expires.

11
00:01:49,248 --> 00:02:00,384
B: I will assign a communications lead and notify business operations through the incident process. Our first stakeholder update will focus on impact and response.

12
00:02:00,984 --> 00:02:12,552
C: Can we set the next technical checkpoint for 14:20 UTC? That gives each track time to gather evidence without delaying an urgent mitigation proposal.

13
00:02:13,152 --> 00:02:26,640
B: Agreed. Escalate material changes immediately between checkpoints, and reassess severity if the measured impact changes. Recovery time remains unconfirmed at this stage.
